1. NON-CUSTODIAL NATURE OF THE APPLICATION\par
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par
Kora Wallet is a fully non-custodial cryptocurrency wallet. This means:\par
\par
  - The developer does NOT have access to your private keys, seed phrases\par
    (recovery phrases), wallet addresses, PIN codes, or any other sensitive\par
    credentials at any time.\par
  - The developer CANNOT initiate, authorize, modify, or reverse any\par
    transaction on your behalf.\par
  - The developer CANNOT recover your wallet if you lose your seed phrase or\par
    PIN. Recovery is solely your responsibility.\par
  - You retain full and exclusive control over your digital assets at all times.\par
\par
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
2. DATA COLLECTION AND PRIVACY\par
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par
Kora Wallet does not collect, transmit, store, or process any personal data\par
on external servers. Specifically:\par
\par
  - All private keys, seed phrases, and wallet credentials are stored\par
    exclusively on your local device using AES-256 encryption.\par
  - No analytics, telemetry, usage statistics, or crash reports are\par
    transmitted to the developer or any third party.\par
  - No personally identifiable information (PII) is collected or processed.\par
  - The application does not use cookies, tracking pixels, or similar\par
    technologies.\par
\par
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
3. BLOCKCHAIN DATA AND THIRD-PARTY SERVICES\par
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\par
To provide wallet functionality, Kora Wallet connects to third-party public\par
blockchain nodes and market data APIs. This involves:\par
\par
  - Transmitting your public wallet addresses to blockchain nodes to retrieve\par
    balance and transaction history. Public addresses are not personally\par
    identifiable in isolation.\par
  - Retrieving cryptocurrency price data from third-party providers.\par
  - No private keys or sensitive credentials are ever transmitted externally.\par
\par
The developer is not responsible for the availability, accuracy, security,\par
or privacy practices of any third-party service or API provider.\par
